// XFAIL: RT-316: (RT-316's family, a while loop) `const C: i64 = { let mut i = 0; while i < 3 { i += 1; } i };` is refused, three times "undefined variable 'i'"; rustc accepts it and prints the EXPECT line (0.30.2)
// From the re-review of g302copy-148 (form pre/q1). Since v0.30.1 at
// least; the release build the same. RT-316 is `loop { break 6; }` as the
// value, refused as "not a compile-time constant"; here the block's local
// is not seen inside the loop (the message differs). Sibling: rt_316c
// (`loop` with a `break`).
// EXPECT: 3
const C: i64 = {
    let mut i = 0;
    while i < 3 {
        i += 1;
    }
    i
};

fn main() {
    println("{}", C);
}
